# `repeat` is copied in line into `main`. What the copied call hands over is text of the very body that is being walked: an element of a list of functions written there. Those closures are expected of the
# copy's parameter: in front of the loop that calls it a test for each, and a build of the loop for each where that pays. Nothing but the unit that is walked is read: no call of another body, no type of
# the rest of the program: so whoever imports what of this file, `main` is compiled the same.
# f1 = repeat, f2 = main
# RUN: walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f3
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=f4
